cosmic-thermostat-b4427dc4.conceptual_definition:
The equation 
\Omega_b h^2 ≃ 0.0224 → 	ext{Matter budget} 
serves as a crucial constraint in Big Bang cosmology, specifically related to baryonic matter. It quantifies the *density* of baryonic matter in the universe, normalized by the critical density and scaled by the Hubble constant squared. This value, derived from observations of the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB) and Big Bang Nucleosynthesis (BBN), is a fundamental parameter that dictates the composition and evolution of the early universe, influencing the formation of light elements and large-scale structures.

